# The demo: `planner --demo` plays this file, a step a line, from the top, with its drawn pointer.
# Edit it as you like - the whole demo is here (the owner, 2026-11-18). It is read from where the
# planner is started (tools/demo/owner.gui); a planner started elsewhere plays the copy built in.
#
# The lines:
#
#   click plan-zoomicon          the pointer to a control, and a click; it waits for the control
#   click map@0.40x0.40          a point in a map: across, then down, as parts of its box
#   click map@0.50x0.50:right    :right after any click is the right button
#   click map@vehicle            the vehicle's place on the map
#   click map@vehicle+80,-80     80 metres east and 80 south of the vehicle
#   screen plan                  wait for that screen to be showing
#   key Escape                   a key: Escape, Return, ctrl+f
#   type 100                     text into what has the keyboard
#   wait tab-simulation 120      wait for a control to come on screen, so many seconds at most
#   wait located 180             ... or for the vehicle: located, armed, climbed, auto
#   answer fly-prompt-ok 3       click it if it comes within so long, else go on
#   pause 2                      seconds
#
# Record your own: run `planner --record` (or --demo), use it normally, and copy the lines it
# prints in the terminal into this file. Typing is not recorded: add a `type` line where you typed.
# A `#` starts a comment. A click whose control does not come within five seconds is passed over
# and the demo goes on; a `wait` that does not come stops the demo, and the status line says which
# line and why.

# ---- The demo as it was while its steps were fixed in the Welcome-Demo-Sitl plugin ----

# The simulator's copter, started from SIMULATION; the planner connects to it.
wait tab-simulation 120
pause 2
click tab-simulation
click sitl-picture-quad
wait located 180
pause 3

# PLAN, and the map brought in on the copter.
click tab-plan
click plan-zoomicon
click menu-zoomToVehicle
pause 1

# Home set where the copter is, from the map's right-click menu: without it Write refuses.
click map@vehicle:right
click menu-setHomeHere
pause 1

# Four waypoints in a square around the copter, 80 metres out.
click map@vehicle+80,+80
click map@vehicle+80,-80
click map@vehicle-80,-80
click map@vehicle-80,+80

# A survey to the west: a polygon drawn on the map, then Auto WP > Survey (Grid) and Accept.
click map@vehicle-240,+0:right
click menu-polygon
click menu-addPolygonPoint2
click map@vehicle-160,+80
click map@vehicle-160,-80
click map@vehicle-320,-80
click map@vehicle-320,+80
click map@vehicle-240,+0:right
click menu-autoWP
click menu-surveyGrid
click survey-BUT_Accept
pause 2

# The mission written to the copter.
click plan-write
pause 2

# FLY: armed, taken off, and sent on the mission.
click tab-fly
click fly-tab-actions
click force-arm
wait armed 20
click takeoff
answer fly-prompt-ok 3      # TakeOff asks the height the first time only
wait climbed 40
click Auto
wait auto 15
pause 2

# ---- The owner's own clicks, as he recorded them ----

click fly-tab-actions
click fly-tab-messages
click fly-tab-actionssimple
click fly-tab-preflight
click fly-tab-gauges
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs
click fly-tab-status
click fly-tab-servo
click fly-tab-servo
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tab-auxfunction
click fly-tab-scripts
click fly-tab-payload
click fly-tab-tlogs
click fly-tab-tlogs
click tab-plan
screen plan
click tab-setup
screen setup
click setup-page-ConfigFirmwareDisabled
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
click setup-page-ConfigFrameClassType
click setup-page-ConfigAccelerometerCalibration
click setup-page-ConfigHWCompass2
click setup-page-ConfigRadioInput
